# {{ display_name }}

Plain Vue 3 + NestJS + PostgreSQL, with TypeScript throughout. NestJS serves Vue
and `/api` from the same process, origin and application image.

```sh
npm ci
npm run db:up
npm run build
SEED_DEMO=true npm start
```

Open http://localhost:3100. Use `npm run dev` to rebuild on source changes, then
reload the browser. `PORT` controls the application port; `HOST` defaults to
localhost. PostgreSQL binds localhost port 55440 and stores data in a named
Docker volume. `POSTGRES_PORT` changes the database port; configure `DATABASE_URL`
to match. `npm run db:stop` stops the development database without deleting data.
Production and CI supply `DATABASE_URL` directly.

`npm start` applies TypeORM migrations before starting Nest. `npm run db:migrate`
applies migrations to an existing build. Schema synchronization is disabled.
Example tasks require `SEED_DEMO=true` and seed once. They are not created by
default in production.

```sh
npm run format
npm run lint
npx playwright install chromium
npm test
```

Tests use a disposable PostgreSQL container, or an explicitly supplied
`TEST_DATABASE_URL`/`DATABASE_URL`, and isolate data in randomly named schemas.
They cover API validation and writes, SPA deep links and missing assets, browser
CRUD/filtering, mobile layout, failure handling, migration idempotence, full
process restarts and development-watch recovery. No database mocks are used.

Build the single application image:

```sh
docker build --build-context application=. -f backend/Dockerfile -t {{ project_name }} backend
```

The shared deployment workflow builds only `backend`; this image contains both
API and frontend. PostgreSQL is deployed using the shared role. `run_e2e: true`
gates CI deployment on browser scenarios. Use the Startup CLI for deployment,
Vault and template updates. No deployment is performed by local setup/tests.

No authentication or analytics is configured. Before public launch add access
control, reviewed operator/privacy information and verified backups/HTTPS.
